From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: L1519 fixes from the T182b check: its word table only with the switch on, a line at the first check

Follows 0982 (EDEN_UP_L1519_FAST_DRAWS, port of zortos293/Lichii PR #1519, commit 65745c2 by
Zortos). Found in the T182b check:
- 0982 put the merged words and the 5x18 range table into HandleWordTable, which EDEN_UP_L1161_DRAW
  allocates and fills per pipeline whatever EDEN_UP_L1519_FAST_DRAWS says: with L1161 on and L1519
  off, about 2.9 KiB more per pipeline (90 empty vectors plus the table) and a sort per slot,
  unlike T181. Now its own table (L1519WordTable), made only with the switch on; TakeReusableDraw
  uses it only when the pipeline has one (else the L1161 check, as T181).
- The count line was written only when a write reached a span: a run where none did showed no line
  at all. It is now also written at the first span check.

Off: as T181 (no table, no work). Not in the kept-store stamp: vk_graphics_pipeline.*,
vk_rasterizer.cpp (KEEPS THE STORE).
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_graphics_pipeline.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_graphics_pipeline.cpp
index a876f4fb14..29c3594c2f 100644
